@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+# app
+
+A small user store over an in-memory database. Run the tests with `npm test`.
+
+## Users API
+
+Import from `src/api/`. Every function takes a `db` (a `Db` from `src/db.js`, migrated with `src/migrate.js`) as its first argument. Calling any of them without `db` throws `<name>: db is required`.
+
+A user object looks like this:
+
+```js
+{ id: '3f0c…', email: 'ada@example.com', fullName: 'Ada Lovelace', createdAt: '2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z', lastLogin: null }
+```
+
+`email` must contain `@` and be unique, ignoring case. `fullName` must be non-blank and at most 100 characters.
+
+### `src/api/users.js`
+
+#### `createUser(db, { email, fullName })`
+
+Creates a user with a new id and the current time as `createdAt`. Returns the new user. Throws if the email is invalid or already in use, or the full name is invalid.
+
+#### `updateUser(db, id, { email, fullName })`
+
+Changes only the fields that are passed. Returns the updated user, or `null` if no user has this id. Throws if a passed email or full name is invalid.
+
+#### `getUser(db, id)`
+
+Returns the user with this id, or `null`.
+
+#### `getUserByEmail(db, email)`
+
+Finds a user by email, ignoring case. Returns the user, or `null`.
+
+#### `countUsers(db)`
+
+Returns how many users there are.
+
+#### `searchUsers(db, query)`
+
+Returns users whose `fullName` or `email` contains `query`, ignoring case, oldest first. An empty query matches every user.
+
+#### `deleteUser(db, id)`
+
+Removes the user. Returns `true` if a user was removed, `false` if no user has this id.
+
+#### `recordLogin(db, id, when = new Date())`
+
+Sets the user's `lastLogin`. Returns the updated user, or `null` if no user has this id.
+
+#### `listUsers(db, { limit = 50, offset = 0 } = {})`
+
+Returns one page of users, oldest first.
+
+#### `importUsers(db, users)`
+
+Inserts users as given, keeping their ids and timestamps. Every user is checked before any is inserted. Throws if a user has an existing id, an invalid or duplicate email, or an invalid full name; nothing is inserted. Returns the inserted users.
+
+### `src/api/export.js`
+
+#### `exportUsersCsv(db)`
+
+Returns every user, oldest first, as CSV with the header `id,email,fullName,createdAt,lastLogin`. Fields containing commas, quotes or line breaks are quoted.
+
+#### `importUsersCsv(db, csv)`
+
+Reads CSV written by `exportUsersCsv` and inserts its users with `importUsers`. Throws if the header or a row is malformed, or if `importUsers` rejects a user; nothing is inserted. Returns the inserted users.
+
+### `src/api/format.js`
+
+#### `displayName(user)`
+
+Returns `user.fullName` when it has non-blank text, otherwise the part of `user.email` before `@`.
diff --git a/src/api/export.js b/src/api/export.js
